#: ../../../advanced/json_type_manifests.md:91
msgid "Notes for the C-side emitter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/json_type_manifests.md:93
msgid "Two things are easy to miss in the SerDes metadata:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/json_type_manifests.md:95
msgid "**`readOnly`**: emit it only for properties that have a Get but no Set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/json_type_manifests.md:96
msgid ""
"**`$ref` vs `object`**: whenever the value type is a `vtk*` pointer, emit "
"`$ref` with the concrete class name; reserve bare `\"type\":\"object\"` for "
"genuinely opaque/unknown types. The `$ref` is what lets `x.getScalarTree()` "
"chain into a typed proxy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/json_type_manifests.md:100
msgid ""
"**`maySuspend`**: OR `FunctionInfo::IsMaySuspend` across the same-named "
"overloads that collapse into one manifest entry, and emit the key only when "
"the result is true. A false value is left implicit to keep manifests lean."
msgstr ""
